Exemption from Stamp Duty Land Tax (SDLT) for Registered Providers of Social Housing
As a result of the changes made, Section 150 of the Finance Act 2013, dealing with the annual tax on enveloped dwellings and relief for providers of social housing, will be amended as follows:

(a) Subsection (2)(a) will be changed to use the term "qualifying" instead of "relevant." The portion of the subsection from "(that" to "landlord)" will be removed.

(b) In subsection (3), the term "relevant" will be replaced with "qualifying" wherever it appears.

(c) Paragraphs (a) to (c) in subsection (4) will be replaced with the following:
  (a) Section 2 of the Finance Act 2003, subsection (2), which applies to a reference to a qualifying housing provider controlled by its tenants, will also apply to a non-profit registered provider of social housing controlled by its tenants;
  (b) "Qualifying body" will refer to:
      (i) Entities described as qualifying bodies in subsection (3) of the Finance Act 2003, section 71;
      (ii) The Scottish Ministers;
      (iii) A council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994;
      (iv) Scottish Homes;
  (c) "Public subsidy" will include:
      (i) Anything considered a public subsidy for the purposes of section 71 of the Finance Act 2003, and for this section, the reference in subsection (5)(a) of that section to "the purchaser" will be understood as a reference to P or the qualifying housing provider;
      (ii) Any grant or other financial assistance under section 18 of the Housing Act 1996 (social housing grants);
      (iii) Any grant or other financial assistance under section 2 of the Housing (Scotland) Act 1988 (general functions of the Scottish Ministers);
  (d) "Qualifying housing provider" will include:
      (i) A relevant housing provider as defined in section 71 of the Finance Act 2003;
      (ii) A body registered as a social landlord in a register maintained under section 1(1) of the Housing Act 1996, designated as Welsh registered social landlords;
      (iii) A body registered under section 20(1) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2010 (Scottish registered social landlords).

Subsection (13) will be retroactively applied, as if it had come into force on 6 March 2024.

