Simplified text: 
Section 17: Academy of Scientific and Innovative Research, 2011
The Academy of Scientific and Innovative Research, 2011
17. Powers of Board.-
(1) The Board is responsible for overseeing, directing, and controlling the affairs of the Academy and has the authority to review the actions of the Senate.
(2) In addition, the Board has the authority to:
a) Make decisions regarding the administration and operation of the Academy;
b) Introduce educational programs at the Academy;
c) Establish regulations;
d) Recruit individuals for academic and other positions at the Academy;
e) Review and amend or revoke Ordinances;
f) Approve annual reports, accounts, budget estimates, and development plans of the Academy for the next financial year;
g) Endorse investments in Academy infrastructure including land and buildings;
h) Perform other duties and exercise additional powers as designated by this Act or the regulations.
(3) The Board also has the authority to appoint committees and conduct inquiries as necessary under this Act.

